{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1878290421337428200', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjo4Njc0MzgyMTE=', 'rest_id': '867438211', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': True, 'can_media_tag': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Oct 08 04:50:19 +0000 2012', 'default_profile': False, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': 'Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me. Jhn 14:6', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 50506, 'followers_count': 2456, 'friends_count': 53, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 21, 'location': '⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ ⭐️ ⭐️', 'media_count': 4211, 'name': 'Charles', 'normal_followers_count': 2456, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1880414782525960361'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/867438211/1688221459', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1801746097783578624/a6uZZVF9_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'Glory2God777', 'statuses_count': 47373, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}, 'professional': {'rest_id': '1652653435278204928', 'professional_type': 'Business', 'category': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1878290421337428200'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1736657908000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '292', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/iphone" rel="nofollow">Twitter for iPhone</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4NzgyOTA0MjEwNjQ4NDczNjA=', 'text': "𝐒𝐡𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐝 𝐎𝐟 𝐓𝐮𝐫𝐢𝐧\n\n²⁹ . . . blessed are they that have 𝑛𝑜𝑡 𝑠𝑒𝑒𝑛, and yet have believed.\n— John 20:29 KJV\n\nThere are biblical reasons why the authenticity of the “Shroud of Turin” is questionable, as it does not align with the teachings of the Bible.\n\n5 reasons why these claims lack authenticity:\n\n𝟏. The Bible states that Jesus’ body was wrapped in linen cloths, not a single shroud, which conflicts with the idea of the Shroud of Turin.\n\n⁷ And the napkin, that was about His head, not lying with the linen clothes, but wrapped together in a place by itself.\n— John 20:7 KJV\n\n𝟐. The Bible describes how Jesus was severely beaten to the point where his appearance was unrecognizable as human. However, the face on the shroud would still be identifiable to those who knew him.\n\n¹⁴ As many were astonied at thee; His visage was so marred more than any man, and His form more than the sons of men:\n— Isaiah 52:14 KJV\n\n𝟑. In Psalm 22, a prophecy is noted regarding Christ, indicating that the Messiah would experience having all of His “bones are out of joint” - However, the image portrayed on the Shroud does not align with the depiction of a man with every bone out of joint.\n\n¹⁴ I am poured out like water, and all my bones are out of joint: my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my bowels.\n— Psalm 22:14 KJV\n\n𝟒. The account provided by John offers crucial details that were omitted in other accounts of Jesus' burial. The passage describes how Joseph of Arimathaea and Nicodemus prepared Jesus' body by wrapping it in linen cloths with spices, totaling about a hundred pounds. The Shroud shows an image of a naked man, inconsistent with the wrapping and spice-packing described in John's account.\n\n³⁹ And there came also Nicodemus, which at the first came to Jesus by night, and brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about an hundred pound weight . ⁴⁰ Then took they the body of Jesus, and wound it in linen clothes with the spices, as the manner of the Jews is to bury.\n— John 19:39-40 KJV\n\n𝟓. The biblical account of Jesus mentions his beard being plucked out, which contradicts the appearance of a full beard on the individual depicted on the shroud.\n\n⁶ I gave my back to the smiters, and my cheeks to them that 𝐩𝐥𝐮𝐜𝐤𝐞𝐝 𝐨𝐟𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐡𝐚𝐢𝐫: I hid not my face from shame and spitting.\n— Isaiah 50:6 KJV\n\nStrong's Number\nH4803\nOriginal Word\nמרט\nTransliterated Word\nmâraţ\nPhonetic Spelling\nmaw-rat'\nParts of Speech\nVerb\n\nStrong's Definition\nA primitive root; to polish; by implication to make bald (the {head}) to gall (the shoulder); {also} to sharpen: - {bright} {furbish} (have his) hair (be) fallen {off} {peeled} pluck off (hair.)\n\nBrown-Driver-Briggs' Definition\n1. to bare, polish, make smooth or bald or bare\n    * (Qal)\n        1. to make bare\n        2. to scour, polish\n    * (Niphal) to be made bald\n\nNote:\nThe lengthy hair depicted in the shroud appears to defy the laws of gravity. Rather than cascading down the man's back as expected, it remains parallel to his body as if he were in a standing position, creating a perplexing visual anomaly.\n\n⁸ It is better to trust in the Lord than to put confidence in man.\n— Psalm 118:8 KJV", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Sun Jan 12 03:58:28 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1878272579720429714', 'display_text_range': [14, 272], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 2, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd 𝐒𝐡𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐝 𝐎𝐟 𝐓𝐮𝐫𝐢𝐧\n\n²⁹ . . . blessed are they that have 𝑛𝑜𝑡 𝑠𝑒𝑒𝑛, and yet have believed.\n— John 20:29 KJV\n\nThere are biblical reasons why the authenticity of the “Shroud of Turin” is questionable, as it does not align with the teachi